silm:instances_papers_09_minimal_category_theory_chapters_01_objects_and_arrows_sections_04_concrete_anchor_survey_concrete_anchor_12_Kilogram#kilogram silm:hasLongDescription "The Kilogram is the SI unit Kilogram, the unit leg of the BodyMassMeasurement99. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Kilogram', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
